      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Let's consider the effect of pressure on a reversible reaction we have encountered before. For the dinitrogen tetroxide/nitrogen dioxide reaction, a shift in the equilibrium position results in a color change, as seen below: "
                  }
                ],
                "id": "ooju3itnal7l0zd",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "fkl32xmdh6lbbpe",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "d19eehoeartgw7p",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "\\underset{\\mathrm{colorless}}{{\\mathrm N}_2{\\mathrm O}_4(g)}\\;\\;\\rightleftharpoons\\;\\;\\underset{\\mathrm{brown}}{2\\; {\\mathrm{NO}}_2(g)}",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": ""
                  }
                ],
                "id": "3381688699",
