      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "30bj6khq32tne47",
                "text": "A Note about Catalysts"
              }
            ],
            "id": "0cn75skt470jp98",
            "type": "h1"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "As we learned during our study of kinetics, a "
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "catalyst"
                  }
                ],
                "content": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "A substance that increases the rate of a reaction without itself being consumed by the reaction."
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "1217478203",
                    "type": "p"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "2050066973",
                "trigger": "hover",
                "type": "popup"
              },
              {
                "text": " can speed up the rate of a reaction. Though this increase in reaction rate may cause a system to reach equilibrium more quickly (by speeding up the forward and reverse reactions), a catalyst has no effect on the value of an equilibrium constant nor on equilibrium concentrations."
              }
            ],
            "id": "vzqj4ln4hqhqy36",
            "type": "p"
          }
        ],
        "id": "4087932315",
